  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental lines from Total Governmental Funds column (p4); Intergovernmental 109,720 split by the all-fund budget schedule's breakdown (p7: highway allocation 80,820, municipal equalization 15,283, motor vehicle fees 5,280, other intergovernmental 8,337; ties exactly). Transfers on p4 are printed only net per fund; governmental total net transfers 44,240 (from proprietary funds) recorded as transfers_in. Business-type from the modified cash basis proprietary statement (p6): receipts = charges for services + interest received; disbursements = operating expenditures + interest expense + payments on long-term debt (equals 359,237 on Statement of Activities p2). The accrual-basis proprietary statements (pp8-10) are supplementary and on a different basis; not recorded (proprietary field null for cash basis). Detail: only supplementary schedule is the combined all-fund budget schedule (p7), so detail is per fund column of the governmental funds statement (p4) and the cash-basis proprietary statement (p6). Balance sheet: assets from Statement of Net Position Totals column; governmental equity from governmental funds statement (totals equal), business-type equity from p1. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
